\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A categorical variable has a finite number of levels; a binary variable has two. A model may be studied by increasing variable cardinalities while fixing its graph, or by increasing the number of variables while fixing cardinality. Transforming between these encodings requires a stated preservation property for distributions or computational tasks.
